WEBVTT

01:30.990 --> 01:35.990
The Rules Say You're Safe,
But Glasses Say You're Out

01:50.460 --> 01:52.510
President? What's this?

01:52.510 --> 01:59.260
Glasses Sugoroku

01:52.940 --> 01:57.090
I found it by the side of the road
on my way to school this morning.

01:57.090 --> 01:59.260
So you picked it up?

01:59.260 --> 02:00.470
Look closely!

02:00.840 --> 02:03.060
It says "Glasses Something-or-Other."

02:03.100 --> 02:04.730
Correct Answer: Glasses Sugoroku

02:04.730 --> 02:06.970
Glasses Something-or-Other?

02:07.540 --> 02:11.220
Throwing away things with "glasses"
written on them is unlawful dumping.

02:09.250 --> 02:11.810
Unlawful Dumping

02:11.220 --> 02:13.210
I couldn't let it pass.

02:13.210 --> 02:15.990
Unlawful dumping is no good.

02:13.750 --> 02:15.990
Unlawful Dumping

02:17.320 --> 02:19.200
It appears to be a game.

02:19.200 --> 02:20.030
That's what "Sugoroku" is.

02:20.030 --> 02:23.030
It looks kind of fun! Let's try it out!

02:30.250 --> 02:32.640
Then, as president, I will go first.

02:37.800 --> 02:39.820
Huh? It moved on its own!

02:39.820 --> 02:42.420
Some words just appeared
in the goal space.

02:43.280 --> 02:46.430
"Your lenses fog up when you wear a mask."

02:47.780 --> 02:48.900
What's going on?!

02:49.780 --> 02:51.690
A mask!

02:54.560 --> 02:56.340
I can't see!

02:56.340 --> 02:57.650
I can see just fine.

02:57.840 --> 03:01.040
So whatever appears in the space
you land on actually happens.

03:01.040 --> 03:02.790
The mask won't come off!

03:02.790 --> 03:03.890
Neither will my glasses.

03:03.890 --> 03:06.750
Do something, Hayato!
You're the only one who can see!

03:06.750 --> 03:10.220
Just a minute! Umm, let's see...

03:10.460 --> 03:15.340
All players must wear glasses.
Glasses may not be removed during the game.
Dice must be rolled in turns.
A player's piece will advance the number of spaces
equal to the sum of the two dice rolled.
When the piece stops on a space, the instructions
for that space will appear in the goal.
All players must respond "I've been there"
to the instructions for that space.

03:10.460 --> 03:15.340
"All players must respond 'I've been there'
to the instructions for that space."

03:15.770 --> 03:17.340
I've been there!

03:21.360 --> 03:23.330
I've been there!

03:28.870 --> 03:32.860
Of course. This is a Glasses
"I've Been There" Game.

03:33.550 --> 03:34.830
Interesting!

03:35.360 --> 03:37.650
Okay! Whose turn is next?

03:37.650 --> 03:39.360
Okay, I'll go.

03:43.070 --> 03:46.860
"You're half asleep, so you wash
your face with your glasses still on."

03:52.250 --> 03:54.070
My hands are moving on their own!

03:56.850 --> 03:58.630
I've been there!

03:59.720 --> 04:02.050
No, I've never done that before.

04:02.050 --> 04:05.880
But I have put in eye drops
while wearing my glasses!

04:06.100 --> 04:06.900
No!

04:08.320 --> 04:09.060
Not again!

04:09.060 --> 04:11.890
Hayato! Just say
"I've been there" already!

04:11.890 --> 04:13.770
I've been there!

04:14.220 --> 04:17.180
"You go to a yakiniku restaurant
and get oil on your lenses."

04:18.020 --> 04:19.490
I've been there!

04:19.490 --> 04:21.410
Huh, really?

04:22.650 --> 04:25.040
It doesn't matter!
Just say "I've been there" already!

04:25.040 --> 04:26.170
I've been there!

04:28.160 --> 04:30.780
"You go to an okonomiyaki restaurant
and get oil on your lenses."

04:30.780 --> 04:32.310
I've been there!

04:32.310 --> 04:33.920
That's basically the same thi—

04:33.920 --> 04:35.130
Hayato!

04:35.130 --> 04:36.410
I've been there!

04:37.640 --> 04:39.570
Whose turn is next?

04:39.570 --> 04:41.170
Yours!

04:43.180 --> 04:47.010
I quit! It's no fun with Hayato here.

04:47.010 --> 04:49.970
He can't help it. His glasses are fake.

04:49.970 --> 04:53.490
I feel sad for him, being unable to say
"I've been there" with the rest of us.

04:53.500 --> 04:55.090
This game has shown me

04:55.090 --> 04:59.100
how unsuited Hayato is to being
part of the Glasses Club!

04:59.730 --> 05:02.440
President! The game's not over yet!

05:02.440 --> 05:04.980
I'll play right, I promise! Please? Please?

05:06.190 --> 05:08.040
My eyes! My eyes!

05:14.420 --> 05:16.640
Huh? It won't open.

05:16.640 --> 05:18.890
Maybe it's just locked?

05:18.890 --> 05:19.930
Get out of the way.

05:21.420 --> 05:23.630
Maybe the frame is off-balance.

05:24.300 --> 05:26.770
We have no choice.
We'll have to go out the other way.

05:26.770 --> 05:28.760
This is bad! This is bad! This is bad!

05:29.030 --> 05:31.140
I've got to let them all know!

05:35.390 --> 05:37.400
It's no use! This one won't open, either!

05:37.400 --> 05:39.900
But it's definitely not locked.

05:39.900 --> 05:44.140
Besides, it's not even time for
the school to be closed yet.

05:46.170 --> 05:48.410
Hey! Open the door!

05:51.130 --> 05:52.040
Hey!

06:01.840 --> 06:02.980
Why?

06:02.980 --> 06:04.440
What's going on?

06:06.960 --> 06:10.010
What are you doing here, brothers?

06:10.320 --> 06:12.260
Because...

06:12.610 --> 06:14.090
...you guys...

06:16.630 --> 06:18.600
...refuse to throw away your glasses!

06:18.600 --> 06:19.680
Huh?

06:19.830 --> 06:22.260
If you throw away your glasses,
you can leave the building!

06:22.260 --> 06:25.220
Glasses Temple Hinge!

06:29.620 --> 06:32.510
Now, throw away your glasses at once!

06:32.510 --> 06:34.690
Glasses Modern Bridge!

06:36.090 --> 06:38.080
What are you doing, brothers?

06:40.040 --> 06:42.460
Takuma! They're impostors!

06:43.090 --> 06:46.370
Anyone who would tell you to throw away
your glasses can't be your brother!

06:46.700 --> 06:49.860
Let's run! Mitsuki, take care of Yukiya!

06:49.860 --> 06:50.820
R-Right!

06:50.820 --> 06:52.050
You won't get away!

06:52.050 --> 06:53.720
Under Temple!

06:54.440 --> 06:55.220
Mitsuki!

06:55.220 --> 06:56.740
Modern Bridge!

06:56.740 --> 06:57.810
President!

06:58.940 --> 07:00.530
President!

07:04.780 --> 07:06.360
Anyway, let's all get out of here!

07:06.360 --> 07:07.290
Right!

07:19.440 --> 07:21.560
What's going on here?

07:21.560 --> 07:23.700
President! Look at this!

07:27.440 --> 07:30.520
"Abandoning the game in progress
is not allowed."

07:30.520 --> 07:33.730
"Failure to comply will result
in glasses retribution."

07:33.900 --> 07:35.280
Glasses retribution?

07:35.280 --> 07:39.130
Is that why my brothers
came after us like that?

07:39.130 --> 07:42.020
It's what we call "reaping what you sow."

07:45.640 --> 07:46.860
Sachie-san!

07:46.860 --> 07:48.620
So give up now.

07:48.620 --> 07:51.010
Throw away your glasses at once!

07:53.660 --> 07:54.770
Hey, hey, hey!

07:54.770 --> 07:56.540
Wh-Why does she have a chainsaw?!

07:58.440 --> 08:04.800
If you refuse to throw them away,
I will slice them into ribbons myself!

08:04.930 --> 08:08.180
I saw this in a horror movie once!

08:11.260 --> 08:13.430
This is no time for laid-back reminiscing!

08:15.170 --> 08:16.320
Run!

08:20.080 --> 08:21.130
Hey!

08:21.490 --> 08:23.770
No running in the halls!

08:24.680 --> 08:27.860
People like you are
unworthy of wearing glasses.

08:31.250 --> 08:32.660
I saw this in a movie, too!

08:39.510 --> 08:41.620
But we're Earthlings!

08:46.490 --> 08:47.590
Run!

08:50.460 --> 08:53.720
Are they all impostors
created by the game?

08:53.720 --> 08:56.480
But why are they all movie references?

08:56.480 --> 09:00.360
Probably because the game
is ripping off a movie, too!

09:14.250 --> 09:15.280
This way.

09:18.660 --> 09:23.160
Soma-senpai, maybe we should
take off our glasses like they said.

09:23.160 --> 09:24.290
Fool!

09:24.700 --> 09:29.290
Just as a warrior's sword is his life,
glasses are our lives!

09:29.590 --> 09:32.300
But those lives are in danger right now.

09:32.810 --> 09:34.550
We'll continue the game!

09:35.560 --> 09:39.290
Of course. The game will end
when someone reaches the goal.

09:39.290 --> 09:43.330
Then the fakes created by
the game might disappear, too!

09:43.330 --> 09:47.240
But I can't say "I've been there"
to any of the glasses experiences.

09:47.240 --> 09:50.320
You'll have to deal with it!
It's the only way.

09:53.800 --> 09:55.200
Whose turn is next?!

10:04.970 --> 10:07.380
"Wearing headphones for a long time

10:07.380 --> 10:10.170
pushes your ears into your frames
and makes them start to hurt."

10:12.220 --> 10:13.340
Ow...

10:13.340 --> 10:15.220
I actually have experience with that!

10:17.970 --> 10:19.420
I've been there!

10:23.050 --> 10:24.680
Okay! Who's next?

10:24.880 --> 10:26.910
"When you put your glasses on in a hurry,

10:26.910 --> 10:28.490
the temple pokes you in the eye."

10:28.490 --> 10:30.000
I've been there!

10:30.000 --> 10:33.360
"Strands of your hair are pulled out
when they get stuck in the hinge."

10:33.360 --> 10:34.690
I've been there!

10:42.040 --> 10:43.930
"You take a face hit in dodgeball

10:43.930 --> 10:47.380
and the rules say you're safe,
but glasses say you're out."

10:47.380 --> 10:48.430
What does that mean?

10:48.430 --> 10:50.170
Here I go, big brother!

10:51.660 --> 10:52.420
Ow!

10:52.720 --> 10:54.660
You all get one, too!

10:58.040 --> 10:59.290
Ow!

11:00.700 --> 11:02.530
I caught the ball, but...

11:04.080 --> 11:05.680
M-My glasses!

11:06.230 --> 11:07.690
Now I get it.

11:08.160 --> 11:09.730
I've been there!

11:11.740 --> 11:13.670
Next is Soma-senpai's turn!

11:13.670 --> 11:16.200
Roll a six and you'll make it to the goal!

11:16.490 --> 11:17.410
Okay!

11:21.090 --> 11:22.940
We know you're there!

11:31.640 --> 11:33.090
Found you!

11:37.010 --> 11:40.720
If you don't want to disappear too,
then throw away your glasses!

11:41.570 --> 11:42.770
President!

11:42.970 --> 11:44.220
Make a decision!

11:45.950 --> 11:49.220
This is the end. Throw away your glasses.

12:13.950 --> 12:16.050
So you've finally decided to see sense.

12:40.420 --> 12:41.530
It's a six!

12:49.970 --> 12:52.200
President! Words are
appearing on the goal!

12:52.200 --> 12:53.200
Read them!

12:55.700 --> 12:58.960
"Despite all that, will you
continue to wear glasses?"

13:03.510 --> 13:04.960
Despite all that, I...

13:05.220 --> 13:05.970
What?

13:07.200 --> 13:08.720
Despite all that, I...

13:09.510 --> 13:12.980
I love glasses!

13:51.980 --> 13:53.560
Looks like the game is complete.

13:57.060 --> 13:58.410
Okay! Let's go home!

13:58.410 --> 13:59.340
Yeah!

13:59.340 --> 14:02.490
Great work, Soma-senpai!

14:11.890 --> 14:13.700
The roof, where no one's around.

14:14.020 --> 14:18.660
Looking down on the students
from here is my secret pleasure.

14:21.360 --> 14:22.980
Glasses Sugoroku?

14:23.540 --> 14:26.110
Who brought this thing here?

14:26.970 --> 14:28.970
I'm confiscating it!

14:30.500 --> 14:33.650
And maybe I'll play it with
the student council later!

14:44.990 --> 14:49.980
When I Look at the Glasses Club,
It Makes Me Think of Us Back Then

15:05.120 --> 15:08.370
What have I done?

15:08.370 --> 15:09.760
It doesn't matter. Just drink.

15:09.760 --> 15:13.110
Teachers are supposed to be role models
for the students. We can't be late.

15:13.110 --> 15:16.900
Just be careful from now on.
Come on, drink!

15:17.110 --> 15:19.650
I can't believe I was late to homeroom.

15:19.650 --> 15:20.400
I'm...

15:22.780 --> 15:24.400
I'm a failure as a teacher!

15:24.570 --> 15:26.900
Just drink and forget about it!

15:32.820 --> 15:35.140
Hotaka-kun...

15:35.140 --> 15:38.760
Why'd you decide to be a teacher?

15:39.720 --> 15:42.250
Hey, did you hear me?

15:42.250 --> 15:44.170
You've had too much to drink.

15:44.660 --> 15:46.170
I think it's time to quit.

15:46.340 --> 15:47.490
Quit?

15:49.210 --> 15:54.060
So, Hotaka-kun, you think
I should quit too, huh?

15:54.520 --> 15:58.020
Okay! Hariu Kyosuke, 24 years old,

15:58.020 --> 16:01.870
will submit his letter of
resignation tomorrow!

16:01.870 --> 16:05.610
Tomorrow's Sunday. C'mon, let's go home.

16:07.870 --> 16:10.320
We're going home! Get down from there!

16:10.320 --> 16:11.320
No.

16:11.320 --> 16:14.570
I'm not going home!
Don't leave me by myself.

16:16.370 --> 16:19.690
Has he always been such a bad drunk?

16:20.120 --> 16:22.130
Closed
Cafe Tet-chan

16:21.560 --> 16:24.750
Tetsu-san! It's me! Shirogane!

16:30.370 --> 16:33.260
Hey, it's Tet-chan.

16:33.260 --> 16:36.270
I'm quitting teaching as of today!

16:40.210 --> 16:41.400
And for you, water.

16:42.500 --> 16:46.410
A farewell gift, huh? Down the hatch!

16:48.850 --> 16:50.270
I don't have any snacks.

16:50.270 --> 16:53.580
He's a little depressed and
doesn't want to go home.

16:53.580 --> 16:56.490
But there's no other places open.

16:56.490 --> 16:57.790
I'm sorry.

16:58.260 --> 16:59.660
It's okay.

16:59.660 --> 17:03.280
I couldn't sleep, so I was up anyway.
I'll hang out with you.

17:03.610 --> 17:07.400
Oh, you two are pretty close, huh?

17:07.400 --> 17:11.170
Just what kinda relationship
you got, anyway?

17:14.160 --> 17:17.120
It happened when I was attending Hima High.

17:20.180 --> 17:24.190
It was my second year.
I was president of the automotive club.

17:24.710 --> 17:26.070
I was a problem child,

17:26.070 --> 17:28.310
always running off half-cocked
and causing trouble.

17:28.530 --> 17:30.300
This should do it!

17:40.600 --> 17:43.500
Each time, I'd get called
to the faculty office,

17:43.500 --> 17:45.620
and the club advisor would
give me a tongue-lashing.

17:46.850 --> 17:49.680
The advisor was Mr. Asahina.

17:49.680 --> 17:51.380
Tetsu-san here.

17:51.560 --> 17:55.140
Oh? You taught at Hima High?

17:56.730 --> 17:58.180
A long time ago.

17:58.660 --> 17:59.900
Then, one time,

17:59.900 --> 18:01.830
the Hima High automotive club

18:01.830 --> 18:04.650
decided to participate
in a solar car contest.

18:05.990 --> 18:09.920
We were so fired up about creating
the world's greatest solar car.

18:20.560 --> 18:21.290
However...

18:22.950 --> 18:25.170
Around that time,
I was in the middle of a feud

18:25.170 --> 18:28.290
with the guys from Kilauea Tech
in the next town over.

18:29.100 --> 18:31.500
The principal is warning everyone

18:31.500 --> 18:34.030
not to start any trouble
before the big contest.

18:34.680 --> 18:37.850
If you start a fight with another school,
you won't be allowed to participate.

18:38.390 --> 18:39.730
So no matter what happens,

18:39.730 --> 18:42.010
don't lay a hand on the guys
from Kila High, okay?

18:42.560 --> 18:45.340
If you do, it's my neck on the line.

18:49.360 --> 18:53.420
What the hell?
He's just worried about himself.

18:55.060 --> 18:58.120
And on the day we finished the solar car...

18:58.610 --> 19:01.870
It's finished! We'll win for sure with this!

19:01.870 --> 19:04.370
Sorry, but it ain't gonna happen.

19:05.430 --> 19:07.800
What are students from
Kila High doing here?

19:07.800 --> 19:09.080
Get out of here now!

19:09.600 --> 19:13.380
Sure, we will! After we wreck that car!

19:13.380 --> 19:15.940
What are you doing?! Stop it!

19:16.380 --> 19:19.920
<i>If you start a fight with another school,
you won't be allowed to participate.</i>

19:20.100 --> 19:21.920
Stop! Don't touch them!

19:22.160 --> 19:23.430
What?!

19:23.960 --> 19:27.010
I won't let you lay one finger on this car.

19:27.010 --> 19:28.940
If you wanna beat on
something, beat on me!

19:29.900 --> 19:31.800
You think you're hot stuff?!

19:31.800 --> 19:34.710
Fine, then! I will!

19:51.000 --> 19:53.130
You idiots!

19:53.130 --> 19:55.210
I told you not to touch them!

20:06.690 --> 20:08.100
Mr. Asahina...

20:14.410 --> 20:16.520
It was all backwards.

20:16.520 --> 20:19.800
After telling the students
not to lay a hand on them,

20:19.800 --> 20:22.240
he started a big fight himself.

20:22.240 --> 20:25.660
Cafe Tet-chan

20:25.840 --> 20:28.940
In the end, you took
responsibility for everything

20:28.940 --> 20:31.070
and penned your resignation.

20:31.070 --> 20:33.900
And we got to participate
in the competition.

20:33.900 --> 20:35.160
Like I told you.

20:36.140 --> 20:39.680
If you started any trouble,
it was my neck on the line.

20:40.080 --> 20:41.680
It made me happy, though.

20:44.520 --> 20:48.390
That's when I made the decision
to become a teacher.

20:52.090 --> 20:55.280
You know, when I look at the Glasses Club,

20:55.280 --> 20:57.690
it makes me think of us back then.

20:58.680 --> 21:01.220
So if anything happens to them,

21:01.220 --> 21:05.180
I'll put my teaching career
on the line to protect them.

21:05.180 --> 21:08.450
Just like Mr. Asahina did for me then.

21:08.450 --> 21:12.450
I told you not to call me that.
Just call me Tetsu-san.

21:12.880 --> 21:16.450
If I ever quit being a teacher,
I'll do it then.

21:16.760 --> 21:18.530
So Kyosuke,

21:18.530 --> 21:22.690
do you still plan to quit being a teacher
just because you were late?

21:27.330 --> 21:28.970
You fell asleep?

21:34.300 --> 21:37.730
Jeez. At least take your glasses off first.

21:34.300 --> 21:40.970
Cafe Tet-chan

23:12.070 --> 23:13.740
Senpai's rimless glasses...

23:13.740 --> 23:17.330
They're not rimless glasses.
They're metal two-point frames.

23:17.330 --> 23:18.820
A teacher needs to speak precisely.

23:18.820 --> 23:20.090
S-Sorry...

23:20.090 --> 23:22.800
By the way, yours are round
Boston celluloid frames, right?

23:23.220 --> 23:25.170
No glasses, no life!

23:31.120 --> 23:33.810
Double bridge. Tomorrow's horoscope:

23:33.810 --> 23:36.730
Eat well, sleep well, play well.

23:36.730 --> 23:38.740
Yeah, that's how it is.
